# devices/pclm10/drivers/display/conf: the display-side hardware of this phone.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver WLED
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.wled.c
	help    the panel's backlight (wled=1): the PM8150L's WLED module at 0xd800, whose master
	help    switch is register 0x46 bit 7. The screen of this port is driven through the boot
	help    firmware's framebuffer, so backboardd's blank request reaches no hardware; this
	help    module is that hardware. A thread follows kern.hakios.screen_backlight (1 lit, 0 dark)
	help    and writes the switch; wled_test=1 adds one blink at startup for bring-up
